    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence presents a genuinely balanced case for JPM. The technical picture is strongly bullish\u2014price sits above all three major moving averages (10 EMA at $190.31, 50 SMA at $184.38, 200 SMA at $158.07), MACD histogram is expanding at 1.12, and the stock is at its 60-day peak with +10.22% 20-day and +12.52% 60-day returns. The fortress-scale balance sheet ($4.09T assets, $336.6B equity) supports the bull case. However, the RSI at 74.99 is the highest in the period, price is above the upper Bollinger Band, and there is a critical data vacuum\u2014no income statement, macro, sentiment, or news data available. The bear's downside case (8.7-12% to the lower Bollinger Band or April low) is as plausible as the bull's upside case (7-10% to $210+). With balanced risk/reward and no earnings or macro visibility, initiating new longs at $195.45 near RSI 75 is not a high-conviction entry. Maintaining the position while waiting for either a pullback to the 10 EMA (~$190.31) or the arrival of earnings/macro data is the prudent course. A hard stop-loss at $185.65 (below the 50 SMA) caps downside risk at approximately 5%.\n\n**Entry Price**: 190.31\n\n**Stop Loss**: 185.65\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-modest weight, no more than benchmark weight until data vacuum is filled or a better entry presents itself.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
